===Etymology 2===
{{unk|en}}; probably connected in some way with Etymology 1.<ref>{{cite-web|year=2016|author=Emilia Terzon|title=Origin of the word donga 'a bit of a mystery' to Australian linguists|work=ABC News (Australia)|titleurl=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2016-09-23/origin-of-word-donga-ongoing-mystery-to-linguists/7871488}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/dɔŋə/|a=Australia}}
* {{audio|en|EN-AU ck1 donga.ogg|a=AU}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Australia}} A transportable [[building]] providing [[accommodation]] for one person, often used on remote work sites or as tourist accommodation.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Susie Ashworth; Rebecca Turner; Simone Egger|title=Western Australia|publisher=Lonely Planet|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=QHsF6Jh7DrIC&pg=PA152&dq=%22donga%22%7C%22dongas%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=-FFCT6DEFMeuiQfRiKy1BA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22donga%22%7C%22dongas%22%20australia%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=152
|passage='''Menzies Hotel''' ([Ph] 9024 2043; 22 Shenton St; s/d $48/65, '''donga''' $75) has old-style hotel rooms as well as - for that real goldfields experience - '''dongas''' (temporary miner′s abode, usually made from corrugated iron), and also serves all meals.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=James Woodford|title=The Dog Fence|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=qNntO4VFNUkC&pg=PA225&dq=%22donga%22%7C%22dongas%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=WVdCT6q7HoeQiAfsrsDlBA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22donga%22%7C%22dongas%22%20australia%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=225
|passage=He not only expects his fence to be perfect, he also expects his '''dongas''' to be the best workman′s huts in Australia, and that is what they are.}}
#* '''2009''', [[w:David Marr (journalist)|David Marr]], ''The Ibdian Ocean Solution'', [[w:Robyn Davidson|Robyn Davidson]] (editor), ''The Best Australian Essays 2009'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=VfCwXaVxtdcC&pg=PA118&dq=%22donga%22|%22dongas%22+australia+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=WVdCT6q7HoeQiAfsrsDlBA&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22donga%22|%22dongas%22%20australia%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 118],
#*: Workers building roads in the bush sleep in '''dongas''' like these and are well paid for their discomfort.

=====Usage notes=====
* Usually used in [[outback]] Australia, especially the northwest.

